WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.903
Threat hunting is a proactive approach to identifying malicious activity that may evade traditional alerting mechanisms.

00:00:06.903 --> 00:00:10.730
Hunters develop hypotheses, investigate multiple data sources, collect evidence,

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.557
and determine whether suspicious activity represents a real threat.

00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:20.085
Even when hunts do not uncover active attackers, they improve visibility, refine detections,

00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:22.636
identify gaps, and strengthen security operations.

00:00:22.636 --> 00:00:26.038
Threat hunting works alongside SIEM, EDR, incident response,

00:00:26.038 --> 00:00:31.140
and threat intelligence to help organizations become more resilient against evolving threats.
